  "residuals": [
    "The tool also counts the stream's stop-propagation handler naming a collector unit (c1 refuses, rc half state); the packet wording names only start lists and failure or success handlers. The tool is stricter than the text.",
    "c1 and rc do not gate the stream's own start and stop hooks; a hook that starts a collector unit would need an edited drop-in and a daemon reload. a03 recorded the stream hooks empty.",
    "Owner summary items 2 and 4 are shorter than GO-C, GO-RC and sections 3.2 and 3.4, which are exact.",
    "systemd 255 forms not observed by d1 (catalog IDs for success, exit, failure and exec-skip entries) fail closed: a different form stops or rolls back, never passes.",
    "If the journal no longer holds the a02 period, c1 stops before any effect at the self-test.",
    "No tool watches the timer or the stream after c6."
  ],
